From 3c15fbe7a6733f109b07c5e00b5704cf4a576296 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HighAsCG Assembly <assembly@highascg.local>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 13:51:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] core: video modes can be added at runtime safely
 (WO-1020)

Prerequisites for AMCP VIDEO-MODE ADD:

- video_format_repository: find/find_format/store/get_max_video_format_size take a
  shared_mutex. The repository is copied by value into the accelerator and the AMCP static
  context but shares one impl, so a runtime store was a data race with every producer and
  AMCP lookup. store() now returns whether the id was new.
- make_custom_video_format_desc(): the <video-modes> checks (id, size, field count 1|2,
  time-scale/duration, cadence summing to 48 kHz, derived cadence for integer rates) as a
  core function. server.cpp switches to it in the AMCP commit, so startup and AMCP apply
  the same checks. Non-numeric cadence is a user_error (startup threw
  std::invalid_argument); the cadence sum is 64-bit.
- same_video_mode(): field-by-field equality, for an idempotent VIDEO-MODE ADD.
- image_mixer: the zero buffer for layer-less frames was a function-local static sized once
  from the boot maximum. A channel on a bigger mode added later (CHANNEL ADD, SET MODE)
  would have read past its end. It is now shared, grown on demand, and each returned array
  keeps the buffer it points into alive.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MxpJi7ZHbr5bkwDuaHmchx
