From 9e243d9b462108f784aecc0c7caa49204813b40c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HighAsCG Assembly <assembly@highascg.local>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 13:52:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] core: routes survive a source mode change and a removed
 source; output::clear (WO-1020)

- route: format_desc is behind a mutex (format_desc()/fps()/set_format_desc()). The source
  channel thread refreshes it on every live route when its stage format changes, so a
  SET MODE on the source no longer leaves routes with the old format (upstream TODO at
  video_channel.cpp route(); audit WO-1016 P-d). Route producers read it every tick in
  set_cross_channel(), hence the lock instead of a plain field. route is no longer movable.
- route::source_removed: set by video_channel::close_routes() (CHANNEL REMOVE). A route
  producer then outputs an empty frame instead of repeating its last frame, whose audio
  would loop as a buzz forever. Routes asked for after close_routes() start closed.
- video_channel::live_route_count(): routes taken from the channel that some producer still
  holds (CHANNEL REMOVE refuses while > 0 unless FORCE).
- output::clear(): drop every consumer at once; each still dies on its own thread through
  destroy_consumer_proxy, as with AMCP REMOVE.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MxpJi7ZHbr5bkwDuaHmchx
