From 2f168f91fb7828e216aa1c1f5f67a1b94cb89583 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HighAsCG Assembly <assembly@highascg.local>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 13:52:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] protocol: LOCK release callbacks no longer capture a raw
 lock_container (WO-1020)

LOCK ACQUIRE binds an object to the client connection whose deleter called
do_release_lock() on a raw `this`. A channel's lock_container used to live as long as the
server, so that was safe; with CHANNEL REMOVE it can die while the client stays connected,
and the client's disconnect would then call into freed memory. The impl is now
shared_ptr-owned and the deleter holds it weakly.

