From 5c3373ec5d40912adac57cec28c06a63743e9d38 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HighAsCG Assembly <assembly@highascg.local>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 13:52:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] amcp: ADD ch[-idx] XML <consumer element> (WO-1020, audit
 WO-1016 P-a/P-b)

Builds the consumer with the preconfigured (casparcg.config) factory instead of the AMCP
parameter one, so every XML option can be applied live: screen always-on-top, stretch,
aspect-ratio, colour-space, linear filter, mipmaps, <slices>; every DeckLink option
(video-mode, pixel-format, buffer-depth, key-device, subregion, ports, ...); artnet and
pixel, which have no AMCP factory at all; ffmpeg realtime.

The element is a single AMCP parameter: quoted XML (escape " as \") or, when it does not
start with '<', base64 of the UTF-8 XML. The index defaults to the consumer's own (as at
startup) and, as with ADD, replaces a consumer already on that index.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MxpJi7ZHbr5bkwDuaHmchx
---
